{0 Runtime APIs}

Workero provides OCaml interfaces to APIs in the Cloudflare Workers runtime,
with helpers for routing and JSON. For configuration and resources accessed
through [env], see {{!page-bindings}Bindings}.

{1 Handlers and routing}

- {{!page-handlers}Handlers}: register HTTP, scheduled, and queue handlers with
  {!Workero.serve}, {!Workero.scheduled}, and {!Workero.queue}.
- {{!page-email}Email}: receive messages from Email Routing with
  {!Workero.email}, then forward, reply to or reject them.
- {{!page-router}Router}: match methods and paths, read route parameters, and
  mount groups of routes.

{1 HTTP and data}

- {{!page-requests}Requests and responses}: read headers and bodies, choose a
  status, and return a response.
- {{!page-fetch}Fetch}: make outgoing HTTP requests.
- {{!page-url}URLs}: read encoded and decoded paths and query parameters.
- {{!page-json}JSON}: parse and decode bodies, return JSON, and convert values
  for JavaScript APIs.
- {{!page-streams}Streams}: read and write bodies in chunks or forward a body.
- {{!page-forms}Forms and file uploads}: read multipart and URL-encoded forms.
- {{!page-websockets}WebSockets}: accept connections and receive messages.
  For hibernating connections, see {{!page-durable_objects}Durable Objects}.
- {{!page-cache}Cache}: read and write cached responses in the local data
  center. Cache uses [caches.default] and needs no [env] binding.

{1 Network}

- {{!page-socket}Sockets}: open outbound TCP connections with
  {!Workero.Socket.connect} and read and write them with streams.
- {{!page-entrypoints}Entrypoints}: expose RPC methods with
  {!Workero.Entrypoint.register} and call them on a service binding.
- {{!page-workflows}Workflows}: write durable multi-step programs with
  {!Workero.Workflow.register} and start them with a Workflow binding.

{1 Execution}

- {{!page-async}Async and background work}: wait for results, run independent
  operations, and use {!Workero.Context.wait_until}.
- {{!page-logging}Logging}: write console entries or use OCaml standard output.
- {{!page-globals}Timers, time, and randomness}: delays, timestamps, random
  bytes, and UUIDs.

{1 Reference}

See {!Workero} for OCaml signatures. Each guide describes the operations
Workero exposes and links to the corresponding platform documentation. The
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/}Cloudflare runtime API reference}
describes the wider platform. Use {{!page-interop}JavaScript interop} for
available operations without a typed wrapper.
